// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 14-control-flow
// facility: rule.control.block [Ref-Binding-Last-Use] (a reference lent to a thread is borrowed through, D-0219, CHG-0258); rule.control.flow-analysis (the spawn row, D-0213); conf.ref-lent-to-thread-lives-to-join
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (static)
//
// `r` is lent to a thread and never mentioned again. Lending it is a
// borrow of `*r` the handle holds until `join` (`spec/14` §6's spawn row),
// so another binding holds a reference borrowed through `r`, and `r` does
// not end at its last use: `deriv(r, x, exclusive)` stays T, and reading
// `x` while the thread may be writing it is refuted.

import std;

fn bump(ref<i32, exclusive> p)
{
    *p = *p + 1;
}

fn main()
{
    i32 x = 1;
    auto r = &mut x;
    auto t = spawn(bump, r);
    printf("%v\n", x);
    join(t);
}
